  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA consisting of NNN integers and an integer XXX. Your goal is to have as many equal integers as possible in the array. To achieve this goal, you can do the following operation:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N)(1 \\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N)  and set Ai=Ai⊕XA_i = A_i \\oplus XAi​=Ai​⊕X,  where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise xor operation.\nFind the maximum number of equal integers you can have in the final array and the minimum number of operations to obtain these many equal integers.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case contains two lines of input.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers N,XN, XN,X.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing two space-separated integers - first, the maximum number of equal integers in the final array and second, the minimum number of operations to achieve these many equal integers.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤X≤1090 \\leq X \\leq 10^90≤X≤109",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (100 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 2\n1 2 3\n5 100\n1 2 3 4 5\n4 1\n2 2 6 6",
        "output": "2 1\n1 0\n2 0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: One way to obtain 222 equal integers is to set A1=A1⊕2A_1 = A_1 \\oplus 2 A1​=A1​⊕2   =1⊕2=3\\; = 1 \\oplus 2 = 3=1⊕2=3. So the array becomes [3,2,3][3, 2, 3][3,2,3]. There is no way to obtain 333 equal integers in the final array.\nTest case 222: There is no way to obtain more than one equal integer."
      }
    ]
  },
